  "instructions": "## The resistor an LED cannot live without\n\nA red LED (forward drop about 2.0 V, rated 20 mA) is connected to 5 V through R1. With R1 too small the LED burns out; too large and it is dim.\n\n## Do this\n\n1. Choose R1 so that the LED current is between **10 mA and 20 mA** (aim for 15 mA). Use the slider or type a value.\n2. Confirm with the ammeter through D1. Measure the voltage across the LED: notice it stays near 2 V whatever the current.\n3. Answer: how much power does R1 dissipate at your chosen value?",
